SUMMARY:Lies\, Likes and LLMs
DESCRIPTION:In a world where information travels faster than ever\, why is trust in facts\, experts\, and institutions collapsing? Vikas Swarup presents a lecture on the crisis of truth in the digital age. \nSocial media platforms reward content that attracts attention rather than accuracy\, while artificial intelligence can now generate persuasive text\, images\, audio\, and video at unprecedented scale. Swarup examines the technological\, psychological\, and societal forces driving this crisis\, its implications for democracy and social cohesion\, and the urgent need to foster critical thinking and digital literacy — including the role institutions like Azim Premji University can play in nurturing informed\, questioning\, and ethically grounded citizens. \nThis lecture is a part of Azim Premji University’s Public Lecture Series. \nPresented by: \n \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nSocial Media\, Artificial Intelligence and the Crisis of Truth\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScZAUI0IgSR70Cfj4iIQ1z9Pn21FKnU4mKFVt_xqDSrPGVylw/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speaker*: Vikas Swarup\n*Event Categories*: Media\, Politics\, Society\, Technology
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/lies-likes-and-llms/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Media,Politics,Society,Technology
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Thumbnail-8.jpg
END:VEVENT
